On Wed, Aug 19, 2015 at 6:18 PM, Ilmen <ilmen.pokebip@gmail.com> wrote:

>
> On 19/08/2015 21:47, Pierre Abbat wrote:
>
>> ni'o lo selbilma be fi la .tsarat. zo'u ko seljde zukte lo se ctuca be lo
>> .elvita jdaca'i .i lo termi'e be ri bei mi cu seldje se zukte ko
>>
>> What is the antecedent of {ri}?
>>
>> Pierre
>>
> If I'm not mistaken, in the case of two or more nested sumti sharing the
> same termination point due to elided terminators, {ri} targets the most
> recently introduced one, so {lo .elvita jdaca'i} in this case. Please
> correct me if this is wrong or inaccurate.


I think that's the rule, except it doesn't matter if the terminators are
elided or not. It would be the same for "lo se ctuca be lo .elvita jdaca'i
ku be'o ku". "ri" targets the already complete sumti that started last.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

